				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				65,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Maintain): Update plist serialization to use XmlWriteOptions\n\nReplace the deprecated `XmlFormat` builder pattern with `XmlWriteOptions` for serializing the `Info.plist` file. This aligns the implementation with the latest `plist` crate API while preserving the required hand-written style (tab indentation, LF line endings).\n\nUpdate imports to expose `XmlWriteOptions` and switch the serialization call to `to_writer_xml_with_options`. Add explicit type annotation for the `Root` variable and adjust comments to reflect the new API usage. The idempotent write logic and trailing newline handling remain unchanged.",
			"SHA": "c9db04d2810b3111e7033d19d2450ba9adf4f263"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-13T22:05:33Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				65,
				3
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Maintain): Replace string-mutation with native plist parsing\n\nThe `PlistEdit` module previously relied on fragile string manipulation and XML-escaping logic to inject the `LSEnvironment` dictionary into `Info.plist`. This approach was prone to whitespace drift and nesting errors.\n\nReplace the custom parser with the `plist` crate to establish a robust parse-modify-serialize pipeline consistent with the `JsonEdit` pattern. The implementation now deserializes the file into an in-memory `Value` tree, updates the `LSEnvironment` key using standard dictionary operations, and re-serializes to XML with deterministic formatting (tab indentation).\n\nUpdate `Error.rs` to expose `plist::Error` and add logic to skip writing if the serialized output matches the existing file. This ensures idempotent builds and prevents unnecessary repository churn while maintaining the exact XML structure required by Apple's LaunchServices.",
			"SHA": "65e8c49e0fef5dda4f7d4ec99e03c9182ad70943"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-13T17:25:30Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				65,
				4
			],
			"Message": "feat(Maintain): Inject runtime environment variables into Info.plist\n\nImplement the `PlistEdit` module to parse and inject an `LSEnvironment` dictionary into `Info.plist` during the build process. This enables dev-control variables (Trace, Record, Inspect, Disable) and runtime configuration to be available when the bundled `.app` is launched via LaunchServices (Finder double-click) without requiring a wrapper script.\n\nThe `Process` orchestration logic now loads values from `.env.Land` (excluding build-time flags) and system environment variables, sanitizes them for XML, and writes the resulting dictionary into the Tauri template. The implementation uses targeted string replacement to preserve the hand-maintained file structure without adding heavy plist parsing dependencies.\n\nThe new constants for Land environment variables are exposed in `Constant.rs` and the module is registered in `Build/mod.rs`.",
			"SHA": "9960c70eaa444a95ae17f0ad6d334a9d532fdf77"
		}
	],
	"TimeStamp": 1781048763252
}